# Data Access Patterns

## Data Access Layer — `src/db/queries/`

All reads and writes must be encapsulated in helper functions inside
`src/db/queries/`, one file per entity (`decks.ts`, `cards.ts`). Never import the
store or touch the document directly from a component or an action.

Helpers stay pure data access: no auth checks, no validation. They take `userId`
as a parameter and filter on it.

```ts
// src/db/queries/decks.ts
export async function getDeckByIdForUser(deckId: number, userId: string) {
  return selectDeckByIdForUser(getSnapshot(), deckId, userId);
}
```

Read logic lives in `src/lib/store/selectors.ts` as pure functions, so pages and
actions share one implementation. The query helper is a thin async wrapper.

## Retrieval

Components read through `useStore(selector)`, which subscribes to the store and
re-renders on change. The selector must be stable — `useCallback` it, or define
it at module scope.

```tsx
const decks = useStore(
  useCallback((db: DbDoc) => selectDecksWithCardsByUser(db, LOCAL_USER_ID), []),
);
```

Check `useStoreReady()` before rendering an empty state. The document loads from
IndexedDB after mount, so "no decks" and "not loaded yet" are different things
and must look different.

Take a one-off snapshot with `getSnapshot()` only when reactivity would be wrong
— the study session does this so that rating a card doesn't remove it from the
list mid-session.

## Mutations

Mutations live in `actions.ts` files. They are plain client functions now, not
Server Actions — there is no server. They keep the same shape as before:

1. `auth()` for the `userId`
2. parse the input with a Zod schema
3. call the query helpers

```ts
export async function updateDeckAction(data: UpdateDeckInput) {
  const { userId } = auth();
  if (!userId) throw new Error("Unauthorized");
  const parsed = updateDeckSchema.parse(data);
  const deck = await updateDeck(parsed.deckId, userId, { ... });
  if (!deck) throw new Error("Deck not found");
  return deck;
}
```

Never take `FormData` as a parameter type — pass typed objects.

There is no `revalidatePath` or `router.refresh()`: the store notifies its
subscribers, so mounted pages re-render on their own. Adding them back would be a
no-op at best.

## Ownership

Every helper filters by `userId`, and card-level helpers verify the card's deck
belongs to the user. `userId` is a constant now, but the filters stay: they cost
nothing, they document intent, and they are what a future multi-user version
would need.

Ownership failures return `undefined` rather than throwing. Callers must check.
